<section class="content" id="activities">

<h3>Section 3: Practical Activities</h3>

<p>Complete at least two of these activities this week.</p>

<h4>Activity A: Practice Lectio Divina with a Gospel Passage</h4>
<p>Choose one of these passages: John 15:1-8 (the Vine and the Branches), Luke 5:1-11 (the Call of Peter), or Mark 10:46-52 (Bartimaeus). Follow the four steps of Lectio Divina:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Lectio (Read):</strong> Read the passage aloud, slowly. Read it twice. Which word or phrase catches your attention?</li>
<li><strong>Meditatio (Meditate):</strong> Sit with that word or phrase. Roll it around in your mind. What is God saying to you through it, right now, in your life?</li>
<li><strong>Oratio (Pray):</strong> Speak to God from your heart. Respond to what you have heard. Give thanks, ask, confess, surrender &mdash; whatever the Word stirs in you.</li>
<li><strong>Contemplatio (Contemplate):</strong> Be still. Rest in God's presence. No words needed. Stay there for at least two minutes.</li>
</ul>
<p>Afterward, write down what you discovered. What was the word or phrase? What happened in your heart?</p>
