<h4>Activity D: Try the Jesus Prayer for One Day</h4>
<p>The Desert Fathers prayed: &laquo;Lord Jesus Christ, Son of God, have mercy on me, a sinner.&raquo; Try repeating this prayer quietly throughout one day. Say it while you wait in line, while you walk, while you work. Let it become the background music of your day. In the evening, write down what you noticed.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>Activity E: Pray One Decade of the Rosary</h4>
<p>Choose one mystery &mdash; joyful, luminous, sorrowful, or glorious. Look up the Scripture passage for that mystery. Read it. Then pray the decade slowly: one Our Father, ten Hail Marys, one Glory Be. While you pray the Hail Marys, keep the scene of the mystery in your mind. Afterward, write one insight from the experience.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>Activity F: Practice the Daily Examen</h4>
<p>At the end of each day this week, take five minutes for the Ignatian Examen:</p>
<ol>
<li>Become aware of God's presence. Ask for light to see the day as he sees it.</li>
<li>Review the day with gratitude. What were its gifts?</li>
<li>Review the day with honesty. Where did you respond well to God's grace? Where did you resist it?</li>
<li>Speak to God about what you have seen. Thank him. Ask forgiveness. Seek his help for tomorrow.</li>
</ol>
